node_modules/
dist/
.svelte-kit/

# tools/ is scratch by default, and the exceptions are listed rather than the scratch,
# because scratch is what keeps arriving: these are one-off probes and screenshot
# harnesses written to answer a single question, and once it is answered nobody runs
# them again. They need a browser binary at a hardcoded path and a running stack, so
# they can never join `just app-check` (which globs ui/scripts/check-*.mjs) and a
# reader who found one would have no way to tell whether it still passes.
#
# What earns an exception is being able to FAIL: a file that exits non-zero can catch a
# regression, and one that prints a JSON report for a human to read cannot. Durable
# checks belong in ui/scripts/ and stay tracked there; the four below are the ones that
# have to live here because of what they need at runtime, or because something tracked
# already depends on them.
tools/*
# Pins the drawer's fit rule (9 claims, non-zero exit), and the shared CDP plumbing it
# imports — a tracked file's import cannot be ignored or the next clone cannot run it.
!tools/verify-drawer-settle.mjs
!tools/scroll-probe/
tools/scroll-probe/*
!tools/scroll-probe/cdp.mjs
# Assert-based guard for src/lib/cost/pricing.ts, which the app no longer renders and
# nothing else covers. Needs no browser; deliberately outside the check-*.mjs glob so
# it does not gate the build, which tracking it does not change.
!tools/pricing-self-check.mjs
# Cited by ui/scripts/check-replay-hotkeys.mjs as where its focus claim was measured,
# so ignoring it would leave a tracked check pointing at nothing.
!tools/scrub-focus-keys.mjs
# Drives the three layers that adopted `dismissable`. check-dismissable.mjs pins the logic
# against a stubbed DOM; only a browser can say whether each site's `keep` selector matches
# the surface it meant, and that the desk's own Escape is still unclaimed.
!tools/verify-dismissable.mjs
# The badge harnesses, tracked with the fix they measure: a language tag pinned against
# a scroller is a thing no assertion about styles can see.
!tools/codebadge-shots/
!tools/scriptbadge-shots/
